<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Novo Brdo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Novo Brdo is a fortress and mining town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>. From the early 14th century it was one of the richest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and gold mines in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, worked by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> miners and trading through Ragusa, and it financed the medieval Serbian state. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> captured it in 1455 after a siege, and its mines then declined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/novo-brdo.jpg" alt="Novo Brdo" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kxjan This file is made available under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication. · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NovoBrdoKosovoAbove.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
